  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programmatic Adjustment Loan 2 (PAL 2)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PAL-2 continues the PAL Program support to the government&apos;s medium term program.  The main objectives are the achievement of average annual growth rates of 4.5-5.0 percent during 2002-05comma the reduction of the poverty rate by half by 2005 compared to 2001comma and the reduction of the unemployment rate from 18.1 percent in 2001 to 12-14 percent in 2005comma while making substantial progress towards EU accessioncomma which it is hoped will occur in 2007.  The medium-term program balances a strategy of private sector-led growth with reducing social exclusion and increasing empowerment to ensure wide participation in growth.  The program consists of five complementary pillars:  &#xb7;   Sustaining structural reforms in the enterprise sector with emphasis on completion of privatization and on the restructuring of the energycomma railwaycomma telecommunicationscomma and water sectors; &#xb7;   Establishing a market-friendly business environmentcomma focusing on reducing entry constraintscomma accelerating exitscomma securing deregulation and reducing regulatory costscomma improving the delivery of public services to businesscomma and improving the competitive environmentcomma including through continuing labor market reform; &#xb7;   Deepening the financial sectorcomma improving the legal framework for lendingcomma completing banking reformcomma and developing financial markets; &#xb7;   Improving public sector governancecomma strengthening public administration capacitycomma improving service deliverycomma reducing corruptioncomma strengthening accountability and transparencycomma strengthening public expenditure managementcomma and increasing the efficiency and effectiveness of the judicial system; &#xb7;   Investing in human capital and strengthening social programscomma improving qualitycomma access and efficiency in education and healthcomma continuing pension reformscomma increasing social assistance effectivenesscomma providing for better integration of the disabled and reducing institutionalization of children.</narrative>
  </description>
